# Fish names and descriptions.

ent-FishAngelfish = angelfish
    .desc = Young Angelfish often live in groups, while adults prefer solitary life. They become territorial and aggressive toward other fish when they reach adulthood.

ent-FishArcticChar = arctic char
    .desc = A cold-water anadromous fish widespread around the Northern Hemisphere of Earth, yet it has somehow found a way here.

ent-FishArmorfish = armorfish
    .desc = A small shellfish native to Tizira's oceans, known for its exceptionally hard shell. Consumed similarly to prawns.

ent-FishBabbelfish = babbelfish
    .desc = Babbelfish are both visually -and- psychically unsettling - their psychic wails damage the minds of those nearby. The effect is negligible on humans, but deadly for fish. It is said that splitting one in two and inserting the pieces into each ear unlocks your psychic potential.

ent-FishBabyCarp = baby space carp
    .desc = A juvenile spawn of the dreaded space carp. Don't let the innocent looks fool you, they're aggressive little bastards.

ent-FishBoned = unmarine bonemass
    .desc = What one could mistake for fish remains, is in reality a species that chose to discard its weak flesh a long time ago. A living fossil, in its most literal sense.

ent-FishBumpy = bump-fish
    .desc = A misshapen fish-thing all covered in stubby little tendrils.

ent-FishCardinal = cardinalfish
    .desc = Cardinalfish are often found near sea urchins, where the fish hide when threatened.

ent-FishCatfish = catfish
    .desc = A catfish has about 100,000 taste buds, and their bodies are covered with them to help detect chemicals present in the water and also to respond to touch.

ent-FishChainsawfish = chainsawfish
    .desc = A very, very angry bioweapon, whose sole purpose is to rip and tear.

ent-FishChasmCrab = chasm chrab
    .desc = The young of the lobstrosity mature in pools below the earth, eating what falls in until large enough to clamber out. Those found near the station are well-fed.

ent-FishChasmCrabIce = arctic chrab
    .desc = A subspecies of chasm chrabs that has adapted to the cold climate and lack of abysmal holes of the icemoon.

ent-FishClownfish = clownfish
    .desc = Clownfish catch prey by swimming onto the reef, attracting larger fish, and luring them back to the anemone. The anemone will sting and eat the larger fish, leaving the remains for the clownfish.

ent-FishClownfishLube = lubefish
    .desc = A clownfish exposed to cherry-flavored lube for far too long. First discovered the days following a cargo incident around the seas of Europa, when thousands of thousands of thousands...

ent-FishDolphish = walro-dolphish
    .desc = Strange bloodthirsty apex predator from beyond. A powerful weapon, but it -hates- being held.

ent-FishDonkfish = donk co. company patent donkfish
    .desc = A lab-grown donkfish. Its invention was an accident for the most part, as it was intended to be consumed in donk pockets. Unfortunately, it tastes horrible, so it has now become a pseudo-mascot.

ent-FishEmulsijack = toxic emulsijack
    .desc = Ah, the terrifying emulsijack. Created in a laboratory, the only real use of this slimey, scaleless fish is for completely ruining a tank.

ent-FishFirefish = firefish goby
    .desc = To communicate in the wild, the firefish uses its dorsal fin to alert others of potential danger.

ent-FishFlumpulus = flumpulus
    .desc = You can hardly even guess as to how this possibly counts as a fish. Inexplicably, you get the feeling that it could serve as a fantastic way to cushion a fall.

ent-FishFryish = fryish
    .desc = A youngling of the Fritterish family of delicious extremophile, piscine lifeforms. Just don't tell 'Mankind for Ethical Animal Treatment' you ate it.

ent-FishFryishFritterish = fritterish
    .desc = A deliciously extremophile alien fish. This one looks like a taiyaki.

ent-FishFryishNessie = nessie-fish
    .desc = A deliciously extremophile alien fish. This one is so big, you could write legends about it.

ent-FishGoldfish = goldfish
    .desc = Despite common belief, goldfish do not have three-second memories. They can actually remember things that happened up to three months ago.

ent-FishGoldfishGill = McGill
    .desc = A great rubber duck tool for Lawyers who can't get a grasp over their case.

ent-FishGoldfishThreeEyes = three-eyed goldfish
    .desc = A goldfish with an extra half a pair of eyes. You wonder what it's been feeding on lately...

ent-FishGoldfishThreeEyesGill = McGill
    .desc = A great rubber duck tool for Lawyers who can't get a grasp over their case. It looks kinda different today...

ent-FishGreenchromis = green chromis
    .desc = The Chromis can vary in color from blue to green depending on the lighting and distance from the lights.

ent-FishGullion = gullion
    .desc = This crystalline fish is actually one of only two known silicon-based lifeforms. It avoids death via oxygen-silicate reactions by organically shielding its exterior, allowing the thick scales to calcify into quartz and diamond, at the cost of rendering the fish functionally blind. How xenomorphs manage is a complete mystery bordering on bullshit.

ent-FishGunnerJellyfish = gunner jellyfish
    .desc = So called due to their resemblance to an artillery shell, the gunner jellyfish is native to Tizira, where it is enjoyed as a delicacy. Produces a mild hallucinogen that is destroyed by cooking.

ent-FishGuppy = guppy
    .desc = Guppy is also known as rainbow fish because of the brightly colored body and fins.

ent-FishHolo = holographic goldfish
    .desc = A holographic representation of a common goldfish, slowly flickering out, removed from its holo-habitat.

ent-FishHoloAngel = holographic angelfish
    .desc = A holographic representation of a angelfish. I got nothing snarky to say about this one.

ent-FishHoloCheckered = unrendered holographic fish
    .desc = A checkered silhoutte of searing purple and pitch black presents itself before your eyes, like a tear in fabric of reality. It hurts to watch.

ent-FishHoloClown = holographic clownfish
    .desc = A holographic representation of a clownfish, or at least how they used to look like five centuries ago.

ent-FishHoloCrab = holographic crab
    .desc = A holographic represantion of a soul-crushingly soulless crab, unlike the cuter ones occasionally roaming around. It stares at you, with empty, beady eyes.

ent-FishHoloHalffish = holographic half-fish
    .desc = A holographic representation of... a fish reduced to all bones, except for its head. Isn't it supposed to be dead? Ehr, holo-dead?

ent-FishHoloPuffer = holographic pufferfish
    .desc = A holographic representation of 100% safe-to-eat pufferfish... that is, if holographic fishes were even edible.

ent-FishJumpercable = monocloning jumpercable
    .desc = A surprisingly useful if nasty looking creation from the syndicate fish labs. Drop one in a tank, and watch it self-feed and multiply. Generates more and more power as a growing swarm!

ent-FishLanternfish = lanternfish
    .desc = Typically found in areas below 6600 feet below the surface of the ocean, they live in complete darkness.

ent-FishLavaloop = lavaloop
    .desc = Due to its curvature, it can be used as make-shift boomerang.

ent-FishLavaloopPlasmaRiver = plasmaloop
    .desc = A lavaloop that has evolved to survive in cold liquid plasma. Can be used as make-shift boomerang.

ent-FishMastodon = unmarine mastodon
    .desc = A monster of exposed muscles and innards, wrapped in a fish-like skeleton. You don't remember ever seeing it on the catalog.

ent-FishMonkfish = monkfish
    .desc = A member of the Lophiid family of anglerfish. It goes by several different names, however none of them will make it look any prettier, nor be any less delicious.

ent-FishMoonfish = zagoskian moonfish
    .desc = A disc-shaped fish native of the less shallow areas of Tizira's oceans, roughly the size of a tuna. Highly prized in lizard cuisine for their large eggs.

ent-FishMoonfishDwarf = dwarf moonfish
    .desc = Ordinarily in the wild, the Zagoskian moonfish is around the size of a tuna, however through selective breeding a smaller breed suitable for being kept as an aquarium pet has been created.

ent-FishMossglob = mossglob
    .desc = This dreaded, malicious, and nearly unkillable glob of moss is rumoured to be nature's revenge against fishermen.

ent-FishNeedlefish = needlefish
    .desc = A tiny, transparent fish which resides in large schools in the oceans of Tizira. A common food for other, larger fish.

ent-FishPerch = perch
    .desc = An all around popular panfish, game fish and unfortunate prey to other, bigger predators.

ent-FishPike = pike
    .desc = A long-bodied predator with a snout that almost looks like a beak. Definitely not a weapon to swing around.

ent-FishPikeArmored = armored pike
    .desc = A long-bodied, metal-clad predator with a snout that almost looks like a halberd. Definitely a weapon to swing around.

ent-FishPlaice = plaice
    .desc = Perhaps the most prominent flatfish in the space-market. Nature really pulled out the rolling pin on this one.

ent-FishPlasmatetra = plasma tetra
    .desc = Due to their small size, tetras are prey to many predators in their watery world, including eels, crustaceans, and invertebrates.

ent-FishPufferfish = pufferfish
    .desc = They say that one pufferfish contains enough toxins to kill 30 people, although in the last few decades they've been genetically engineered en masse to be less poisonous.

ent-FishRatfish = ratfish
    .desc = A rat exposed to the murky waters of maintenance too long. Any higher power, if it revealed itself, would state that the ratfish's continued existence is extremely unwelcome.

ent-FishSacabambaspis = sacabambaspis
    .desc = A jawless fish ought to be extinct by the end of the Ordovician period. Some speculate alien intervention may have been behind its survival and inevitable evolution as a dweller of hot springs.

ent-FishSandCrab = burrower crab
    .desc = A sand-dwelling crustacean. It looks like a crab and tastes like a crab, but waddles like a fish.

ent-FishSandSurfer = sand surfer
    .desc = A bronze alien "fish" living and swimming underneath faraway sandy places.

ent-FishSkinCrab = skin crab
    .desc = "And on the eighth day, a demential mockery of both humanity and crabity was made." Fascinating.

ent-FishSlimefish = aquatic slime
    .desc = Kids, this is what happens when a slime overcomes its hydrophobic nature. It goes glug glug.

ent-FishSludgefish = sludgefish
    .desc = A misshapen, fragile, loosely fish-like living goop, the only thing that'd ever thrive in the acidic and claustrophobic cavities of the station's organic waste disposal system.

ent-FishSludgefishPurple = purple sludgefish
    .desc = A misshapen, fragile, loosely fish-like living goop. This one has developed sexual reproduction mechanisms, and a purple tint to boot.

ent-FishSockeyeSalmon = sockeye salmon
    .desc = A fairly common and iconic salmon endemic of the Pacific Ocean. At some point imported into outer space, where we're now.

ent-FishSoul = soulfish
    .desc = A distant yet vaguely close critter, like a long lost relative. You feel your soul rejuvenated just from looking at it... Also, what the fuck is this shit?!

ent-FishSquid = squid
    .desc = An elongated mollusk with eight tentacles, natural camouflage and ink clouds to spray at predators. One of the most intelligent, well-equipped invertebrates out there.

ent-FishStarfish = cosmostarfish
    .desc = A peculiar, gravity-defying, echinoderm-looking critter from hyperspace.

ent-FishStarfishChrystarfish = chrystarfish
    .desc = This is what happens when a cosmostarfish sneaks into the bluespace compartment of a hyperspace engine. Very pointy and damaging - leading cause of spaceship explosions in 2554.

ent-FishStingray = stingray
    .desc = A type of ray, most known for its venomous stinger. Despite that, They're normally docile, if not a bit easily frightened.

ent-FishSwordfish = swordfish
    .desc = A large billfish, most famous for its elongated bill, while also fairly popular for cooking, and as a fearsome weapon in the hands of a veteran spess-fisherman.

ent-FishTadpole = tadpole
    .desc = The larval spawn of an amphibian. A very miniscule, round creature with a long tail it uses to swim around.

ent-FishZipzap = anxious zipzap
    .desc = A fish overflowing with crippling anxiety and electric potential. Worried about the walls of its tank closing in constantly. Both literally and as a general metaphorical unease about life's direction.

fish-trait-amphibious-name = Amphibious
fish-trait-amphibious = This fish has developed a primitive adaptation to life on both land and water.
fish-trait-antigrav-name = Anti-Gravity
fish-trait-antigrav = This fish will invert the gravity of the bait at random. May fall upward outside after being caught.
fish-trait-anxiety-name = Anxiety
fish-trait-anxiety = This fish tends to die of stress when forced to be around too many other fish.
fish-trait-camouflage-name = Camouflage
fish-trait-camouflage = This fish possess the ability to blend with its surroundings.
fish-trait-carnivore-name = Carnivore
fish-trait-carnivore = This fish can only be baited with meat.
fish-trait-crossbreeder-name = Crossbreeder
fish-trait-crossbreeder = This fish's adaptive genetics allows it to crossbreed with other fish species.
fish-trait-electrogenesis-name = Electrogenesis
fish-trait-electrogenesis = This fish is electroreceptive, and will generate electric fields. Can be harnessed inside a bioelectric generator.
fish-trait-emulsijack-name = Emulsifier
fish-trait-emulsijack = This fish emits an invisible toxin that emulsifies other fish for it to feed on.
fish-trait-emulsijack_psychic-name = Psychic Aura
fish-trait-emulsijack_psychic = This fish emits an almost unblockable psychic aura that assaults minds, slowly killing all nearby fish and making humanoids have a bad time.
fish-trait-hallucinogenic-name = Hallucinogenic
fish-trait-hallucinogenic = This fish is coated with hallucinogenic neurotoxin. We advise cooking it before consumption.
fish-trait-heavy-name = Demersal
fish-trait-heavy = This fish tends to stay near the waterbed.
fish-trait-ink-name = Ink Production
fish-trait-ink = This fish possess a sac that produces ink.
fish-trait-lubed-name = Lubed
fish-trait-lubed = This fish exudes a viscous, slippery lubrificant. It's recommended not to step on it.
fish-trait-mixotroph-name = Mixotroph
fish-trait-mixotroph = This fish is capable of substaining itself by producing its own sources of energy (food).
fish-trait-necrophage-name = Necrophage
fish-trait-necrophage = This fish will eat carcasses of dead fish when hungry.
fish-trait-no_mating-name = Mateless
fish-trait-no_mating = This fish cannot reproduce with other fishes.
fish-trait-nocturnal-name = Nocturnal
fish-trait-nocturnal = This fish avoids bright lights, fishing and storing in darkness recommended.
fish-trait-parthenogenesis-name = Parthenogenesis
fish-trait-parthenogenesis = This fish can reproduce asexually, without the need of a mate.
fish-trait-picky_eater-name = Picky Eater
fish-trait-picky_eater = This fish is very picky and will ignore low quality bait (unless it's amongst its favorites).
fish-trait-predator-name = Predator
fish-trait-predator = It's a predatory fish. It'll hunt down and eat live fishes of smaller size when hungry.
fish-trait-recessive-name = Recessive
fish-trait-recessive = If crossbred, offsprings will always be of the mate species, unless it also possess the trait.
fish-trait-revival-name = Self-Revival
fish-trait-revival = This fish shows a peculiar ability of reviving itself a minute or two after death.
fish-trait-shiny_lover-name = Shiny Lover
fish-trait-shiny_lover = This fish loves shiny things and money, shiny lure recommended.
fish-trait-stinger-name = Stinger
fish-trait-stinger = This fish is equipped with a sharp stringer or bill capable of delivering damage and toxins.
fish-trait-stunted-name = Stunted Growth
fish-trait-stunted = This chrab's development is stunted, and will not properly reach adulthood.
fish-trait-territorial-name = Territorial
fish-trait-territorial = This fish will start attacking other fish if the aquarium has five or more.
fish-trait-toxic-name = Toxic
fish-trait-toxic = This fish contains toxins. Feeding it to predatory fishes or people is not recommended.
fish-trait-toxic_carpotoxin-name = Carpotoxic
fish-trait-toxic_carpotoxin = This fish contains carpotoxin. Definitely not safe for consumption.
fish-trait-toxic_barbs-name = Toxic Barbs
fish-trait-toxic_barbs = The stinger or bill of this fish is coated in a simple, yet effective venom.
fish-trait-toxin_immunity-name = Toxin Immunity
fish-trait-toxin_immunity = This fish has developed an ample-spected immunity to toxins.
fish-trait-vegan-name = Herbivore
fish-trait-vegan = This fish can only be baited with fresh produce.
fish-trait-wary-name = Wary
fish-trait-wary = This fish will avoid visible fish lines, cloaked line recommended.
fish-trait-yucky-name = Yucky
fish-trait-yucky = This fish tastes so repulsive, other fishes won't try to eat it.
fish-evolution-armored_pike-conditions = The fish needs to have the stinger trait
fish-evolution-chainsawfish-conditions = The fish needs to be unusually big and territorial
fish-evolution-dwarf_moonfish-conditions = Requires the moonfish to be small enough.
fish-evolution-fritterish-conditions = Fryish will grow into it over time.
fish-evolution-lubefish-conditions = The fish must be fed lube beforehand.
fish-evolution-mastodon-name = ???
fish-evolution-mastodon-conditions = The fish (and its mate) needs to be unusually big both in size and weight.
fish-evolution-moonfish-conditions = Requires the dwarf moonfish to be big enough.
fish-evolution-nessie-name = ???
fish-evolution-nessie-conditions = The final stage of fritterfish growth. It gotta be big!
